The deck is deliberately split in half. One half is cheap NON-HUMAN bodies whose only job is to attack; the other half is expensive HUMANS you never intend to cast. Winota converts the first into the second — every non-Human that attacks digs six cards deep and puts a Human onto the battlefield already attacking and indestructible. Count your non-Human attackers before combat, because that number is how many free Humans you get.

# The commander
Winota, Joiner of Forces :: every non-Human creature that attacks looks six deep and cheats a Human into play tapped, attacking and indestructible. Four mana, and a board of four tokens is four free Humans.
Reconnaissance :: the best card in the deck. Attack with everything, let Winota trigger on each non-Human, THEN remove the fragile attackers from combat and untap them. You keep the triggers, lose nothing to blockers, and still have blockers up.
Deflecting Swat :: free with your commander out, and it redirects the removal spell aimed at Winota mid-combat.
Giver of Runes :: protection from a colour every turn, for one mana, on the creature that matters.
Flare of Fortitude :: free if you sacrifice a white creature. Your life cannot change and everything you control gains hexproof and indestructible — it beats a wrath, a burn spell and a targeted removal spell at once.

# The non-Human trigger engine
These are not filler. Each one is a Winota trigger every combat.
Goblin Rabblemaster :: a hasty Goblin at the beginning of combat, every turn, and it forces them to attack.
Legion Warboss :: the same effect, and mentor grows whatever it attacks alongside.
Loyal Apprentice :: a hasty flying Thopter each combat while you control your commander.
Ainok Strike Leader :: a Goblin per opponent whenever it or Winota attacks — three extra triggers in a four-player pod.
Anim Pakal, Thousandth Moon :: Gnomes equal to her counter total, every attack, snowballing.
Myrel, Shield of Argive :: Soldier tokens equal to your Soldier count on every attack, and opponents cannot interact during your turn at all.
Okoye, Dora Milaje Leader :: two Soldiers on arrival, and your attacking tokens get first strike.
Phoenix Chick :: one mana, flies, has haste, and it climbs back out of the graveyard whenever you attack with three creatures.
Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer :: a Monkey, so it triggers Winota, and it steals a card and a Treasure on the way through.
Ornithopter :: zero mana, flies, and it is a Winota trigger from turn one.
Phyrexian Walker :: the same, on the ground.
Ornithopter of Paradise :: a trigger that also fixes your mana.
Hope of Ghirapur :: a flying trigger that shuts off an opponent's noncreature spells for a turn.
Quicksilver, Brash Blur :: can start the game on the battlefield, has haste, and is not a Human.

# The Humans you want to hit
Blade Historian :: attacking creatures have DOUBLE STRIKE. Cheated in mid-combat, it doubles the damage of the attack that put it there.
Angrath's Marauders :: all your damage is doubled. Alongside Blade Historian your tokens hit for four times their printed power.
Combat Celebrant :: exert it and you untap everything and get an ADDITIONAL COMBAT PHASE — which is a whole second round of Winota triggers.
Lena, Selfless Champion :: a Soldier for every nontoken creature you control, and she sacrifices to make the team indestructible.
Myrel, Shield of Argive :: doubles your Soldier count and locks opponents out of your turn.
Anim Pakal, Thousandth Moon :: better cheated in than cast, because she starts making Gnomes immediately.
Lightning, Army of One :: once she connects, every source you control deals DOUBLE damage to that player until your next turn.
Grand Abolisher :: nobody can respond to anything for the rest of your turn.
Boromir, Warden of the Tower :: counters anything cast for free, and sacrifices to make the board indestructible.
Professional Face-Breaker :: a Treasure per combat damage step, convertible into impulse draws.
Black Widow, Agile Avenger :: menace, and she grows and draws off the table's extra draws.

# Finding the pieces
Imperial Recruiter :: any creature with power 2 or less — which is most of your non-Human triggers.
Recruiter of the Guard :: any creature with toughness 2 or less.
Ranger-Captain of Eos :: finds a one-drop, and sacrifices to stop every noncreature spell for a turn. That is how you protect the alpha strike.

# Taxing them while you set up
Archon of Emeria :: one spell per turn each, and their nonbasics enter tapped. A token deck barely notices; a combo deck dies to it.
High Noon :: the same lockout on an enchantment, and it converts into five damage later.
Deafening Silence :: one noncreature spell per turn each, and it never touches your creature deployment.
Drannith Magistrate :: no casting from graveyards, exile or the command zone. It turns off every other commander at the table.
Aven Mindcensor :: flash him onto a fetchland or a tutor.
Aven Interrupter :: flash, exiles a spell outright, and taxes what they try to recast.
Charismatic Conqueror :: everything they play either arrives tapped or gives you a lifelinking Vampire.
Hexing Squelcher :: your spells cannot be countered and your creatures get ward.
Esper Sentinel :: taxes their first noncreature spell every turn.
Ocelot Pride :: a Cat every end step you gained life, doubled once you have the city's blessing — and Cats are not Human.

# Removal and protection
Path to Exile :: one mana, exile.
Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd :: flash, and every attack exiles a blocker or a problem permanent for the turn.
Flare of Fortitude :: the free save.
Reconnaissance :: also a defensive card — remove your attackers from combat and they are untapped blockers on the crack-back.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep cheap non-Humans. Ornithopter, Phyrexian Walker and Phoenix Chick look like nothing and are the entire engine — a turn-four Winota with three non-Humans already attacking is three free Humans on turn four.
Do not cast the Humans. Blade Historian, Angrath's Marauders and Lena are all far better cheated in mid-combat, and casting them wastes both the mana and the surprise. If you must hard-cast something, cast a trigger body instead.
Attack with everything, then use Reconnaissance. The Winota triggers happen on declaration, so pulling a 1/1 out of combat afterwards costs you nothing and saves the body for next turn.
Combat Celebrant :: the highest-value hit in the deck. An extra combat is another full round of Winota triggers, and the Humans you already cheated in are untapped for it.
